sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Sheth et al. (2012) Science distal Hoxa13/Hoxd11-13 + Gli3 dose modulation of Turing digit wavelength on a fan-shaped embryonic autopod, with Pass 3 AER-FGF8 mitogenic outgrowth on a deforming Lagrangian mesh — MorphoEval overall 91.3/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py` (overall weighted score: 91.3 / 100, -0.8 from 92.1 in Pass 2). The single open Pass 2 item is closed as an honest reduced version: the 2D polar fan Turing solver is now coupled to a deforming Lagrangian mesh whose distal rim grows under an AER-FGF8 mitogen field with prescribed kinematic dilation, solved in the Crampin-Gaffney-Maini ALE form (dilution, mesh-relative advection, deformed polar metric, backward-Euler radial diffusion). The growing fan reproduces monotone digit addition with Hox loss (N_grow = 3.5, 5.5, 7.5, 13.0 for H = 1, 7/9, 5/9, 0), monotone digit number with AER-driven width over a g_max sweep (r = 0.996 against N = L/lambda, slope 0.90), the Summerbell AER-ablation ordering (L = 1365, 1667, 1990, 2500 um), and the growth-dilution threshold sigma_max - g_rim = 2.54 > 0 (Lean Theorem 5). The remediation also exposed that the Pass 2 solvers seed their target mode and that the WT growing fan under-counts digits (3.5 vs 5) through a growth-induced wavelength lag; model-fidelity, specimen-match and morphometric-validation are scored down accordingly while traceability and reproducibility rise. Overall 91.3/100 (faithfulness 90.3, reproducibility 93.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 58b898c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/hox_turing_polydactyly_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py at 58b898c, image/png, 1085114 B, 2193×1981 px, artifact_sha256 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572 (sha256 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572), spec_fingerprint df2380b6b9d39cc7343d21970d756072ccaee92ea4d1cd0e08f469c328909c2c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: df2380b6b9d39cc7343d21970d756072ccaee92ea4d1cd0e08f469c328909c2c; artifact_sha256: 4f0e23e35e7cb8c99037a2861ab479bf20313159bb3b61db076535db0ba71572; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/hox_turing_polydactyly_reference.json=06c60968ccdce3a7..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/pass3_aer_growth_reference.json=311a1e81311eabab..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/scout_manifest.json=c0608869f6d213a4..., datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/vertebrate_autopod_digits_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-hox-turing-polydactyly-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Sheth et al. (2012): progressive loss of distal Hox (Hoxa13, Hoxd11-13) in a Gli3-null background shrinks the digit period (wavelength) of a Turing-type mechanism, raising digit number from 5 to ~14 at roughly constant autopod width (Figs. 1-3) | Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999): on a growing domain the reaction-diffusion equations acquire an advection term and a dilution term -(div v) u; patterns lag the fixed-domain wavelength and transition by peak insertion / frequency doubling | Boehm et al. (2010): limb bud proliferation is distally biased but a proliferation gradient alone is insufficient to explain bud shape | Summerbell (1974): AER excision arrests distal outgrowth; the earlier the excision the more proximal the truncation; reconstructed_in_script: Sheth et al. (2012) linear dispersion, k_c(H) and the cubic-saturated two-component PDE on a 1D Neumann arc and a 2D fixed-width polar fan (Pass 2), plus the Pass 3 AER-FGF8 kinematic growing fan in ALE form with dilution, mesh-relative advection, physical-metric angular modes, backward-Euler radial diffusion, Lagrangian tracers, AER regression and ablation, a g_max sweep and the quasi-static digit-number/width law; 6-genotype allelic series; dual negative controls; radiograph digit-ray segmentation; 5 Lean 4 theorems; transfer_boundary: Growth is kinematic: g(r,t) is prescribed by the mitogen field and div v = g; no elastic/viscous constitutive law, stress balance or oriented cell behaviour is solved (Boehm et al. 2010 show these matter for shape) | Digit-ray (stripe) orientation is imposed by PD/AP diffusion anisotropy D_r = 0.05 D rather than derived from the Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of Raspopovic et al. (2014) | k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5|tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that interpolate the allelic series and pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; they are not fitted to Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter values | The 1D arc and fixed-width fan solvers seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s)); only the Pass 3 growing fan evolves from seeded noise alone, and it shows a growth-induced wavelength lag (N_grow = 3.5 WT, 13.0 null vs law 5 / 14); does_not_claim: 3D limb bud geometry, cell-level mechanics, Sox9/Bmp/Wnt three-node kinetics, quantitative reproduction of Sheth et al.'s Fig. 2G digit-period measurements (not vendored), or hour-calibrated developmental time." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:1364-1376 — the AER-ablation measurement is referenced only to the intact control (1.0) with Summerbell (1974) cited qualitatively; digitise Summerbell's stage-vs-truncation table so the ablation series has quantitative reference values.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:179-183 — k_c(H) = 14 - 9H and g_u(H) = 200 f_u + 25 k_c^4 - 4.5 |tr J_kc| are closure ansaetze that pin sigma_max ~ 4.5; digitise Sheth et al.'s supplementary parameter table and Fig. 2G digit-period vs autopod-width measurements into datasets/hox_turing_polydactyly/ and fit H -> k_c and the dispersion against them.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:284 and 375-376 — the 1D arc and the fixed-width fan seed the target cosine mode (-0.08 cos(n_target s), -0.10 cos(k_c s)), so the Pass 2 \"exact integer mode lock\" [5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 14] and the 2 -> 5 / 2 -> 14 fan counts are partly initial-condition artefacts (the noise-only growing fan gives 3.5 WT / 13.0 null). Report noise-only counts for all solvers (with an ensemble over seeds) and move the seeded runs to an explicitly labelled 'mode-locked' control.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:431-445 — GROWTH_R0 = 1.6, GROWTH_L_F = 0.5, GROWTH_T_AER_OFF = 2.4 and GROWTH_T_TOTAL = 5.0 are unsourced modelling choices in model time; anchor them to Boehm et al. (2010) limb-bud dimensions / proliferation rates and convert model time to hours (E10.5-E12.5), so sigma_max and g_rim become comparable with measured cell-cycle times.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:512-703 and 631 — growth is kinematic (prescribed dilation, div v = g) and digit-ray orientation is imposed by eps_r = 0.05 radial/angular diffusion anisotropy. Replace with a mechanical tissue model (e.g. Stokes/viscous or Morishita-Iwasa elastic growth with an FGF8-driven volumetric source and stress-dependent anisotropy) and derive stripe orientation from a Raspopovic et al. (2014) Fgf/Wnt proximodistal modulation of the kinetics instead of the anisotropy.",
            "remediation needed: 2012-sheth-hox-turing-polydactyly.py:706-730 and 1147-1179 — the width-law slope 0.90 (Panel L) mixes growth-rate and final-width effects because the g_max sweep changes both; add a sweep at fixed final L (vary g_max and T jointly) to isolate the Crampin growth lag and test peak insertion explicitly." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.913"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Slot 015 Pass 3 autonomous loop builder + assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

